# Generated by crates/ov-app/build.rs from installer-hooks.nsh.in, with the
# model file paths baked in. Edit the .in template, never this.
crates/ov-app/installer-hooks.nsh

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- Tauri
# `crates/ov-app/gen/` is regenerated by tauri-build on every compile. Committing
# it produces a permanent, meaningless diff on the schema files and a merge
# conflict every time two branches build.
crates/ov-app/gen/

# ------------------------------------------------ Models and user data
# Never commit weights: hundreds of megabytes, not ours to redistribute, and a
# repo containing them cannot be cloned casually.
/models/
*.bin
*.onnx
*.ct2
*.pt
*.safetensors
*.gguf

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Local dev
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
/fixtures/audio/*.wav
!/fixtures/audio/.gitkeep

# Working notes from AI-assisted design sessions.
#
# These are scaffolding for the tooling used to build the project, not documents a
# contributor needs. The durable decisions they informed live in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
# and docs/adr/, which are versioned deliberately.
#
# NOTE: .gitignore only affects *untracked* files. If any of these is still in the
# index, the pattern below does nothing for it until you run:
#     git rm --cached PRODUCT.md DESIGN.md docs/UI-RESEARCH.md
# And either way, anything already committed stays in the repository's history.
PRODUCT.md
DESIGN.md
docs/UI-RESEARCH.md
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
# Design-critique snapshots. Same reasoning: they quote PRODUCT.md, the private
# marketing-site brief and audience analysis, so they belong with the planning
# documents above rather than in a public repository.
.impeccable/
# Working plans and audits. Same category again: written to be executed and then
# thrown away, and they quote the private documents freely. What survives one of
# these belongs in docs/adr/ or CHANGELOG.md, which are versioned on purpose.
docs/plans/
docs/superpowers/

# Scraper scratch. Cached responses from research runs, regenerated on demand and
# meaningless to anyone who did not make the query.
.firecrawl/

# Screenshots of other people's applications, gathered while designing against
# them. Reference for the person doing the work, not something to redistribute —
# see the trade-dress note in docs/adr/0010 and the design spec.
docs/reference/

